# Cellular Networks — Simple Point-Form Notes

 ## 1\. Basic Structure of a Cellular Network

 A **cellular network** has two main parts:

 - **RAN — Radio Access Network**
- **Mobile Core**

 ### Simple diagram

```
        Mobile Phone / UE
               │
        Wireless Radio
               │
        ┌──────▼──────┐
        │     RAN     │
        │   eNB / gNB │
        └──────┬──────┘
               │
        ┌──────▼──────┐
        │ Mobile Core │
        └──────┬──────┘
               │
          Internet /
        Other Networks
```

 ### Easy way to remember

 - **RAN = Radio connection**
- **Core = Network control \+ Internet connection**

---

 # 2\. RAN — Radio Access Network

 The **RAN** connects the user's mobile device to the mobile core using a wireless connection.

 ### Main job of RAN

 - Manages the **radio spectrum**.
- Makes efficient use of available radio frequencies.
- Provides good **Quality of Service (QoS)**.
- Connects mobile devices to the core network.
- Handles communication between the **UE** and the core.

 ### Important terms

 - **UE (User Equipment)** = mobile phone, tablet, IoT device, etc.
- **Base Station** = equipment that communicates wirelessly with the UE.
- **4G base station = eNodeB / eNB**
- **5G base station = gNB**
- **gNB = next Generation Node B**

 ### Easy memory

 > **UE → RAN → Core → Internet**

---

 # 3\. Mobile Core

 The **Mobile Core** is the central part of the cellular network.

 ### Main jobs

 - **Authenticates** devices.
  - Checks whether the user/device is allowed to use the network.
- Provides **Internet/IP connectivity**.
- Supports:
  - Data services
  - Voice services
- Makes sure users receive the required **QoS**.
- Tracks the **location/mobility** of users.
- Helps maintain service when a user moves between cells.
- Tracks user usage for:
  - Billing
  - Charging

 ### Mobile Core names

 - **4G:** Evolved Packet Core (**EPC**)
- **5G:** 5G Core / Next Generation Core (**5GC / NG-Core**)

 ### Easy memory

 > **Core = Authentication + Internet + Mobility + QoS \+ Charging**

---

 # 4\. Main Difference Between RAN and Mobile Core

 | RAN | Mobile Core |
| --- | --- |
| Handles radio communication | Handles network services |
| Connects UE wirelessly | Connects users to Internet/services |
| Manages radio resources | Manages authentication |
| Uses eNB in 4G | Uses EPC in 4G |
| Uses gNB in 5G | Uses 5G Core in 5G |
| Handles handover between cells | Tracks user mobility |

### Very simple example

 When you open YouTube:

```
Phone
  ↓
gNB (RAN)
  ↓
5G Core
  ↓
Internet
  ↓
YouTube
```

