 # 14\. SCTP and GTP

 Two important protocols appear in the RAN/Core connection.

 ## SCTP

 **SCTP = Stream Control Transmission Protocol**

 ### Used for

 - Control Plane signaling

 ### Think of SCTP as

 > **SCTP = Signaling**

 It is a transport protocol designed to carry signaling information and has features useful for telecom networks.

---

 # 15\. GTP

 **GTP = GPRS Tunneling Protocol**

 ### Used for

 - User Plane traffic
- Tunneling user data

 It commonly runs over **UDP/IP**.

 ### Think of GTP as

 > **GTP = User data tunnel**

---

 # 16\. SCTP vs GTP

 | Feature | SCTP | GTP |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Main use | Control/signaling | User data tunneling |
| Plane | Control Plane | User Plane |
| Purpose | Carries signaling | Carries user packets through tunnels |
| Common transport | IP | UDP/IP |
| Easy memory | Signaling | Tunnel |

### One-line answer

 > **SCTP carries control-plane signaling, while GTP is used to tunnel user-plane traffic.**

